# Point Taken

Point Taken is a local Windows issue tracker. A person reports a problem in a connected application. A coding agent works on issues from a checkout of the project. The first connected application is Xcmd.

## Start a report

Install Point Taken once on the computer. Start the tray utility at Windows sign-in by default. Keep user data in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\PointTaken`. Read the picker shortcut from `config.json`. Its default value is `Ctrl+F12`. Each adapter handles the shortcut while its application has focus.

A single left click opens or activates the issue list immediately. Open it on the monitor where it was last visible, including after a restart. If there is no saved monitor or it is disconnected, use the monitor under the pointer. Place the window at the right edge and use the full height of the work area. When the list is already open, briefly highlight its border. A right click opens a menu with **Issues…** and **Exit**.

